# Prose-checking fixture. Comments are not prose: recieve teh speling here.
:: harbour_arrival default

> speaker=rhea portrait=concerned caption="Teh door creaks open" @rhea_arrival
  I recieved your letter this morning.

  The lamps in Vexmoor were already lit
  when the ferry docked.

> speaker=narrator bind=(count:int=$letters_remaining) @letters_left
  You have one letter left.
  | You have {count} letters left.

> speaker=rhea bind=(name:string=$player_name) @greet_player
  [slow]Welcome back, {name}.[/slow] The tide turned an hour ago.

> speaker=hazel bind=(item:string=$item_name) @hazel_offer
  Take a {item} for the road.

> speaker=hazel @hazel_ledger
  Keep the \{ braces \} out of the ledger.

> speaker=hazel @hazel_cafe
  The café serves naïve tourists — Zoë pours the coffee herself. 🙂

> speaker=rhea @rhea_prompt
  Where should we go first?

  ? @go_market
    To the market. It is an short walk.
    -> market

  ? @go_inn
    The inn by the quay.
    -> END

:: market
> @market_stalls
  [The stalls are shuttered. A gull watches from the awning.]

:if baker_open()
  ? @buy_bread
    Buy bread from the baker.
    -> END
:else
  ? @leave_market
    Leave the market befre dark.
    -> END
